cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Thailand Central Law Portal consultation participation census,
  2020-2026
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or code, please cite it using these metadata.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Sittikong
    given-names: Badeesorn
    affiliation: >-
      School of Information Technology, King Mongkut's University of
      Technology Thonburi
abstract: >-
  A complete census of public consultations published on Thailand's Central
  Law Portal (law.go.th), the channel made mandatory by the Act on
  Legislative Drafting and Evaluation of Law B.E. 2562 (2019) in
  implementation of section 77 of the 2017 Constitution. 5,572
  consultations posted between December 2020 and September 2026, of which
  5,371 had closed at collection, run by 293 agencies and recording
  1,780,449 responses. Includes the collection and analysis code and a
  record of the collection.
keywords:
  - public consultation
  - regulatory governance
  - Thailand
  - e-participation
  - open government data
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-09-22
